.TH MIRI_FM 1 "October 2026" "libmirisdr-6" "User Commands"
.ad l
.ss 12 0
.SH NAME
miri_fm \- demodulate FM, AM and SSB with a Mirics based receiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B miri_fm
.B \-f
.I frequency
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B miri_fm
tunes a receiver built on the Mirics MSi2500 and MSi001, such as the SDRplay
RSP1, RSP1B, RSPdx\-R2 and RSPduo, demodulates what it hears and writes the
audio as signed 16 bit mono samples, little endian. Without a file, or with
.BR \- ,
the audio goes to standard output. Play it with
.BR play (1)
or
.BR aplay (1),
as in the examples below.
.PP
Frequencies and rates take the suffixes k, M and G, so 24k is 24000.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " frequency"
The frequency to tune to. Give
.B \-f
more than once to scan the frequencies, which needs a squelch. A range such as
.B 118M:137M:25k
scans from 118 to 137 MHz in steps of 25 kHz.
.TP
.BI \-M " modulation"
.B fm
(the default),
.BR wbfm ,
.BR am ,
.BR usb ,
.B lsb
or
.BR raw .
.B wbfm
is short for
.BR "\-M fm \-s 170k \-o 4 \-A fast \-r 32k \-l 0 \-E deemp" .
.B raw
writes I and Q as pairs of signed 16 bit numbers, at the rate it prints.
.TP
.BI \-s " rate"
The rate of the demodulated channel. The default is 24k.
.TP
.BI \-r " rate"
Resample the audio to this rate. By default it stays at the rate of
.BR \-s .
.TP
.BI \-g " gain"
The total tuner gain in units of 10 dB, so 4.5 is 45 dB. The nearest gain the
band has is taken. The default is the library's, 43 dB.
.TP
.BI \-l " level"
The squelch level, as the RMS of the channel with full scale at 16384. The
default is 0, no squelch.
.TP
.BI \-t " delay"
How long the squelch waits, in buffers of about 20 ms. The default is 10. A
positive value mutes the audio or moves on to the next frequency. A negative
value ends the program.
.TP
.BI \-o " factor"
Oversampling, from 1 to 16. The default is 1, and 4 is recommended.
.TP
.BI \-p " ppm"
The error of the reference in parts per million, to correct the tuning. The
default is 0, or the value at the end of the serial when it ends in a number
followed by p.
.TP
.BI \-E " option"
Turn on an option. Give
.B \-E
more than once for more than one.
.B edge
tunes to the lower edge of the channel,
.B dc
removes the DC offset,
.B deemp
adds de\-emphasis and
.B direct
turns on direct sampling.
.B offset
is accepted but does nothing.
.TP
.BI \-i " if"
The IF in Hz.
.B auto
(the default) takes 450 kHz, or 1620 kHz for a channel wider than 480 kHz.
0 is zero IF, which needs a rate of 1.3 Msps or more. 450000, 1620000 and
2048000 are the low IFs, which take any rate. The demodulator then runs at a
whole multiple of the audio rate and averages it down.
.TP
.BI \-w " bandwidth"
The IF filter in Hz. It defaults to the widest the IF allows. 200000 and 300000
need the 450 kHz IF, 600000 any low IF and 1536000 zero IF or the 1620 or
2048 kHz IF. Zero IF also takes 5000000 to 8000000 in 1 MHz steps. A filter the
IF cannot have is refused.
.TP
.BI \-F " size"
A filter with less leakage when the rate is brought down, of size 0 or 9. Size 0
has a poor roll off. It works with zero IF only, a low IF has filters of its own.
.TP
.BI \-A " method"
How the phase is worked out:
.B std
(the default),
.B fast
or
.BR lut .
.TP
.BI \-m " format"
How samples are packed on the USB:
.B 504
(8 bits, the fastest),
.B 384
(10 bits plus 2),
.B 336
(12 bits) or
.B 252
(14 bits). By default the format with the most bits that fits is taken.
.TP
.BI \-e " mode"
The USB transfer,
.B ISOC
(the default) or
.BR BULK .
1 and 2 are taken as ISOC and BULK.
.TP
.BI \-d " receiver"
Which receiver to open: an index counting from 0, the serial of the receiver,
or the start of its serial. The default is 0.
.TP
.BI \-T " board"
The board, when the USB ids do not tell it: 0 a plain MSi2500 and MSi001 board,
or the SDRplay RSP1, 1 the original libmirisdr\(aqs SDRplay plan (its board is
not known), 2 the RSP1B, 3 the RSPdx\-R2, 4 the RSPduo and 5 the Mirics TV reference design
(TV sticks such as the Hauppauge WinTV 133559LF).
.SH EXAMPLES
Listen to an FM station:
.PP
.RS
miri_fm \-M wbfm \-f 96.3M | play \-r 32k \-t raw \-e s \-b 16 \-c 1 \-V1 \-
.RE
.PP
Scan the air band with a squelch:
.PP
.RS
miri_fm \-M am \-f 118M:137M:25k \-l 70 | aplay \-r 24k \-f S16_LE \-t raw \-c 1
.RE
.PP
Decode pagers with multimon:
.PP
.RS
miri_fm \-f 466.025M \-s 22050 | multimon \-t raw /dev/stdin
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR miri_sdr (1),
.BR miri_eeprom (1),
.BR play (1),
.BR aplay (1)
.PP
